==Question #10==
{{Cquote2|My only concern is after a while, high-level players may want to just farm the harder bosses for enjoyment but would be gated behind Orb drops. What are your thoughts on this?}}

[https://youtu.be/9NrVrzYd7EM&t=2070s Youtube Time Stamp]

* '''Mod Arcane:''' For a high-level main, they can buy the Orbs. So they gate it behind them - depends on the price point. But if you generally want to farm them for enjoyment, then you definitely can - they won't be bad to do. The goal would be to have a higher unique chance on them; it might not necessarily be higher uniques per hour. It's not like you're going to be getting screwed or anything like that. If you're an Ironman player that really wants to farm on these harder bosses, then it's just going to be the same as every other problem Ironman has - you've got to work for your resources.
* '''Mod Goblin:''' Yeah, it is what it is coming from me, who only plays Iron these days. My instant thought when somebody is like, "What about me as an Ironman?" is "De-iron!". I only play Iron, but that's what I signed up for! The game is also infinitely easier for me as an Iron now than it was when I made the account. If you don't like it, don't do it or change game modes. I don't think the Orbs are going to be so crazy rare as well; you won't be spending like 200 hours per attempt.
* '''Mod Arcane:''' The idea would probably be like you might be able to get an Orb every hour or so, maybe two hours - if you're grinding hard efficiently - not really rare or anything.
* '''Mod Goblin:''' For me, it's one thing that also adds stakes. If I've done 100 of a boss and I've gotten like two of these Awakener's Orbs, it's like, "Damn, I spent all this time, and now I've got my attempts! I've watched all my videos, I've looked through my Discord for the weird niche methods and streamables from people named after Pokémon, and I've got these 50 kills worth of my time up at stake!". I think that's cool.
* '''Mod Arcane:''' Thankfully, for an Ironman, you solve your own problems somewhat; because, for an Ironman, you're probably going to get hundreds of KCs at each of these bosses and netting in a bunch of Orbs passively. Then once you've finished all your grinds, you've got all your rings, you've got your Virtus, you've got the axe; you're like, "Okay, I've got a stack of Orbs. Let's see if I can do this!". If you then proceed to send all of your Orbs and fail every attempt, every single boss, you should have prepared more. That's part of the game mode - it makes it even more prestigious when you get it under Ironman. If you see that, you know that they grinded for their own Orbs.
* '''Mod Goblin:''' Maybe I'm out of touch, or maybe it is a bigger complaint about what needs changing, but we'll see. I feel like the balance on them should be pretty good, to be honest. And again, to be at this point anyway, where you really care, you'll want to be an Iron with full Torva. So you're probably used to just enduring pain.

==Question #11==
