==Question #15==
{{Cquote2|Are the quest versions still doable for questers/non-aspirational gamers?}}

[https://youtu.be/9NrVrzYd7EM&t=2538s Youtube Time Stamp]

* '''Mod Arcane:''' They will definitely be a challenge. I'd like to believe they're as hard as Vanstrom was when you originally did Vanstrom. They expect you to have slightly higher stats than what Vanstrom is going to expect.
* '''Mod Arcane:''' You can do Vantstrom with a base 70s. It'll be a rough time, but you can just about do it. The higher stats you have, the better. If you're going in with max combat stats, you're gonna have a much more comfortable time, especially gear too.
* '''Mod Arcane:''' I wouldn't be going into these bosses of the 70s and expecting a good time. You can kill them, but you're going to want to be good, and you're going to want a handful of attempts to figure out what's happening.
* '''Mod Arcane:''' They're going to be hard; they're probably going to be the hardest quest bosses we've ever released. We're probably going to keep doing that every time a new Grandmaster quest comes out - I imagine if the quest focuses on combat, we'll probably level it up. We're always going to be pushing you guys harder and better.
* '''Mod Arcane:''' It's important that we do that as well. I think Old School has quite a big problem right now in terms of the gulf between a more casual Skiller that is creeping into PvM, like doing Barrows, maybe towards jumping into Vorkath and doing all these Grandmaster quests.
* '''Mod Arcane:''' Then there's an even bigger gulf between those and doing more difficult bosses like Zulrah, and then eventually, ToB and raids. Hopefully, then these bosses as well.
* '''Mod Arcane:''' There are quite a lot of big gaps. They're not very smooth. ToA did a pretty good job in terms of allowing someone to come in at a pretty low level. Then they just keep piling on Invocation after Invocation, and it gets smoother and smoother, a bit harder and a bit harder. And people can ease themselves quite naturally into PvM. We can do more of it.
* '''Mod Arcane:''' I do think quest bosses are a really good place for that. A quest forcing you to do some PvM gets you out of your comfort zone a bit and gets you more comfortable with things like that. Then actually killing the bosses post-quest may feel a bit more palatable, eventually going into raids. We've released a lot of PVM content in the past four or five years and if you're not interested in PVM at all, that's a lot of content you're missing out on.
* '''Mod Arcane:''' It is our job to get you guys more comfortable with us - hopefully in nice ways. We don't want just to throw you in the deep end and force you to do ridiculous content.
* '''Mod Arcane:''' We're not going to release a quest that's as hard as Inferno, but it is our right to push you guys a bit to get a bit more comfortable step by step. Sometimes we miss the mark and push a bit too hard. Then I'm like, "Oh God, this is too much of a leap", and maybe we nerf the quest versions of the bosses in accordance to that. Maybe you guys have that feedback on the launch. But overall, I think we should be trying to push it a bit.
* '''Mod Goblin:''' It's an interesting one. There are a lot of people who obviously want Quest Cape for the Lumbridge Elite, but are a little bit scared of it getting more difficult.
* '''Mod Goblin:''' At the same time, somebody in chat says "the get good era begins". I don't think it was quite that abrasive an approach, but there's a lot of PvM, and there are a lot of people who definitely have a lot of anxiety about getting into PvM.
* '''Mod Goblin:''' It's finding meaningful and interesting ways to pipeline people into caring about PvM in the first place and helping them build up the fundamentals such as movement presses, prayer switches, gear switches and flicking to some degree and then being able to juggle all of them at the same time while understanding the tick system etc. and being able to introduce them in a meaningful way.
* '''Mod Goblin:''' Pipelining them into caring about PvM is something we should try to do and then get better at doing, I think. Having players do a quest that raises the ceiling, especially with the same gravitas as DT2. It's an interesting way to do it.

==Question #16==
{{Cquote2|Are there one-shot mechanics in the new bosses?}}

[https://youtu.be/9NrVrzYd7EM&t=2798s Youtube Time Stamp]

* '''Mod Arcane:''' I don't think there is anything that straight up just does 99 damage or anything; there's a lot of mechanics that will hit very hard if you mess them up. The Muspah can hit you for around 68 or thereabouts with his magic attack or just a basic flick, so there are definitely things that can do a lot of damage.
There is one mechanic - it’s not really a one-shot mechanic - if you mess up enough times, then you die. You can only make a finite amount of mistakes.
* '''Mod Goblin:''' I will say that anyone doing a blind run of DT2 on a Hardcore on day one is much braver than I would be. I would not advise it!

==Question #17==
{{Cquote2|What does the loot table look like? Is it more like God Wars or Muspah?}}

[https://youtu.be/9NrVrzYd7EM&t=2861s Youtube Time Stamp]

* '''Mod Arcane:''' It’s more like God Wars. I know; there was an era where everyone was asking for God Wars-style drop tables for ages. We then released Nightmare, and players screamed.
* '''Mod Arcane:''' I'm not saying we delivered it accurately back then. We took that feedback on board and tried to deliver something like that then. I think Nightmare succeeded in the regard of having a fairly pitiful loot table, weighting it towards higher uniques.
* '''Mod Arcane:''' It failed in the regard of those uniques being really, really rare. The boss kills took quite a long time, the walk also took a long time; re-gearing was a bit of a pain due to Relicym's Balm and Sanfew Serum. There were a lot of individual things that made the Nightmare grind a bit of a pain. I don't think these bosses have any of that. They just have low resource drops and reasonable unique rates, but also, the uniques, I'm going to assume, will be really expensive.
* '''Mod Arcane:''' Everyone's going to want the new Berserker Ring, right? The Berserker Ring is owned by almost everyone watching this stream. I'd like to think everyone will also want this new ring. They might not be able to afford it, but they will want it, so the demand should be high for many of these rings. It's behind the Grandmaster quest, I’d imagine the supply is not going to be as high as ToA or something like that. Anyone can do ToA; it doesn't really have many requirements.
* '''Mod Arcane:''' These uniques will be worth a lot of money. They're not ridiculously rare or anything like that, but the regular resources will be pretty low. Expect to make less than 3 mil an hour passively like Muspah or Vorkath.

==Question #18==
{{Cquote2|How long will the quest take?}}

[https://youtu.be/9NrVrzYd7EM&t=2986s Youtube Time Stamp]

* '''Mod Arcane:''' I honestly don't know. We've done a lot of playtests. We held an all-day playtest, and no one actually completed it. This is probably going to be a full-day quest for some people, which might be six or seven hours for others. Once a quest guide comes out, it may take three or four hours.
* '''Mod Arcane:''' The vast majority of the stream will probably wait, but there are four bosses and four areas with their own individual puzzles and cutscenes. There’s a lot - it's a really good quest!
* '''Mod Arcane:''' There are a lot of demi-bosses as well. It's not full, like Vardorvis or Duke, but you have these individual bosses who take up a bit of time. It will depend on how much you fail as well; if you really struggle with one of the bosses, that will make the quest a lot longer.
* '''Mod Arcane:''' Same with the puzzles. If you really struggled with the Secrets of the North puzzles, you'll probably need help with the Gorak puzzle. I'm sure the quest guide will solve all your problems!
* '''Mod Goblin:''' On release day, don’t spacebar it! The dialogue is really good, the worldbuilding is good, and the lore is good. Old School has really good lore and really cool world-building.
* '''Mod Goblin:''' Quests are one of the things that makes Old School stand out versus other MMOs in this space because we do quests so differently to a lot of other games where quests are basically just the Slayer skill in different settings.
* '''Mod Goblin:''' Many people view quests as a vehicle to obtain rewards, power and content. They don't care about the quest themselves, but so much time and love has been put into the quest and it's really cool, it’s really good!
* '''Mod Goblin:''' If you can stomach it, don't spacebar it. Don’t use a guide; it's a cool quest. You'll feel good.
* '''Mod Arcane:''' For context, the most fun I’ve ever had in this game was Song of the Elves on release day. I had no idea what was happening, and figuring out the puzzles was so fun! I love that so much, and I’ve never experienced that same magic since I work here now and know all the answers to every quest - it’s spoiled for me. So please, enjoy them!

